From 22ba6824a204ca62b4a26a0faccf966a8a3fc055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: size combined image planes from the accepted
 height

The 8160x6120 NV12 mode needs 9180 luma-stride rows in its single
allocation. Limiting that allocation to twice the old 4096-row PIX
enumeration height truncates the buffer, even though the accepted image
height and separate Y/C write-master heights are valid.

Use twice the existing 8191-row image bound for combined semi-planar
storage. Keep image dimensions unchanged. TFE980 FD uses separate WM7/8
for Y/C; the official piano driver declares 9312x16384 for that output.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 7ebbed354f4..bbd773eeefe 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -23,8 +23,11 @@
 #define CAMSS_FRAME_MIN_HEIGHT		1
 #define CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_HEIGHT_RDI	8191
 #define CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_HEIGHT_PIX	4096
-/* luma plus chroma lines of a 4:2:2 semi-planar frame */
-#define CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_LINES_PIX	(2 * CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_HEIGHT_PIX)
+/* A single memory plane can hold full-height luma and chroma.
+ * Bound the combined allocation by the accepted image height, not the
+ * older PIX enumeration limit: each hardware write master has its own height.
+ */
+#define CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_LINES_PIX	(2 * CAMSS_FRAME_MAX_HEIGHT_RDI)
 
 /* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Helper functions
